title "Stellar life cycle"
layout radial root=star
page a3
font 8pt..34pt wrap=16em

style formation color=#1565C0
style stable color=#2E7D32
style endpoint color=#6A1B9A

node star "Star" .stable
| self-gravitating sphere of plasma
| hydrostatic balance: pressure offsets gravity
node cloud "Molecular cloud" .formation
| cold gas and dust; dense and opaque
| collapse begins when gravity beats pressure
node collapse "Gravitational collapse" .formation
| density rises as the cloud contracts
| gravitational potential becomes thermal energy
node protostar "Protostar" .formation
| heating core before sustained fusion
| jets and disks carry away angular momentum
node fusion "Nuclear fusion" .stable
| hydrogen -> helium releases energy
| luminosity balances radiated energy
node mainseq "Main sequence" .stable
| core hydrogen burning is the long stable phase
| mass controls luminosity and lifetime
node lowmass "Red giant" .stable
| shell burning expands the outer envelope
| helium core becomes degenerate
node white "White dwarf" .endpoint
| compact carbon-oxygen remnant
| electron degeneracy supports it
node massive "Supernova" .endpoint
| explosive death of a massive star
| shock enriches the surrounding medium
node neutron "Neutron star" .endpoint
| ultra-dense remnant supported by neutron pressure
node blackhole "Black hole" .endpoint
| collapse beyond the escape threshold
| event horizon hides the central remnant
node nucleosynthesis "Heavy elements" .endpoint
| fusion and supernovae change chemical composition
| later stars inherit enriched gas
node evidence "Observational evidence" .endpoint
| spectra reveal temperature and composition
| Hertzsprung-Russell diagram organizes populations

cloud -> collapse
collapse -> protostar
protostar -> fusion
fusion -> mainseq
mainseq -> star
star -> lowmass
lowmass -> white
star -> massive
massive -> neutron
massive -> blackhole
massive -> nucleosynthesis
white -> nucleosynthesis
cloud ..> evidence "spectra"
star ..> evidence "luminosity and color"
nucleosynthesis ..> cloud "recycled material"

require star at center
prefer cloud at top-left weight=2
prefer white at bottom-left weight=2
prefer blackhole at bottom-right weight=2
prefer evidence near star within=18em weight=2
